.DS_Store
evals/results/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# uv-lock in the shared pre-commit config regenerates this on every run, because a
# pyproject.toml exists here. It is meaningless: this repo ships skills, not a
# package, and the pyproject holds nothing but tool settings. The generated lock
# declares requires-python ">=3.12", which nobody chose and which contradicts the
# py311 target set for ruff above it. Ignoring it is better than committing a
# version claim no one made.
uv.lock
